  "entity_raw": {
    "name_raw": "Cursed Item Detection",
    "definition_type_raw": null,
    "source_book_raw": "Dungeoneer's Handbook pg. 12",
    "definition_raw": "Source Dungeoneer's Handbook pg. 12\nYour arcane prowess is so great that even cursed items fail to befuddle you.\n\nPrerequisites: Spellcraft 5 ranks, ability to cast detect magic as a spell or spell-like ability.\n\nBenefit: You gain a +2 bonus on checks made to identify the properties of magic items. In addition, you need only exceed the DC of these checks by 5 in order to determine whether or not an item is cursed.\n\nNormal: Unless the check made to identify a cursed item exceeds the DC by 10 or more, the item’s curse cannot be detected.",
    "links_raw": [
      {
        "anchor_text_raw": "Dungeoneer's Handbook pg. 12",
